            "title": "RTR (Ready to Run)",
            "answer": "<p> This normally means that you get everything in the box which you need to be able to run your boat. In some instances you may require AA batteries for your radio or transmitter otherwise you will have everything you need. Please note that many of the sailing boats will still need to be assembled.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_UWHrLT": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "ARTR (Almost Ready to Run)",
            "answer": "<p> This means that you have most of what you need in order to run your boat except you will need to purchase a separate battery (or batteries for some) along with a charger to charge the battery. We can supply the batteries and chargers you will need.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_r4w99E": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "PNP (Plug and Play)",
            "answer": "<p> This version is normally available for the experienced RC user who may alreadyhave most of their own equipment. These versions will require the separate purchase of batteriesand chargers along with the radio and receiver to control the boat. Everything else you need will befound in the box.</p>"
          }
        }
